--
dropped the body
--
unordered_set<K>::insert followed by vector<K> (dog-fooding
src/util/find_symbols.cpp, which uses unordered_set<irep_idt> and
std::vector<irep_idt>): instantiating the unordered_set first used to
leave vector<K> incomplete ("symbol '_Tp_alloc_type' is unknown"), so
v[0] read an arbitrary value.  The fixes: a member class template of a
class template instance is registered in the instance's scope even when
an earlier member fails ([temp.inst]/11, `__alloc_traits<..>::template
rebind<T>', cpp17_member_template_completed_instance), and substitution
starts afresh for each candidate ([temp.deduct.general]/1,
cpp17_push_back_after_unordered_set_decl).
